        <ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-left: var(--space-4);">
          <li><strong>Test the Emergency Shutoff Angle Stop Twice Annually:</strong> Calcium deposits in Mesa water can seize the valve stem. Turn the oval handle behind your toilet gently back and forth once every six months to keep it moving smoothly.</li>
          <li><strong>Perform an Overnight Tank Dye Test:</strong> Place three drops of dark food coloring in the tank before bed without flushing. If color seeps into the bowl by morning, your flapper is leaking and wasting water.</li>
          <li><strong>Avoid Corrosive Chemical In-Tank Drop-Ins:</strong> Blue or bleach chlorine tablets degrade internal rubber seals, warp flappers, and corrode brass bolts within months, causing premature leaks.</li>
          <li><strong>Verify Bowl Stability:</strong> Place gentle pressure on the rim with your hands. If the toilet shifts or rocks even a fraction of an inch, have the closet flange inspected before the seal fails completely.</li>
        </ul>
